=== 3b. THE TAIL, IRF(300)/IRF(100) -- A COMPARISON (was gate 12b) ===
  ⚠ Same status as section 3: reported, not gated. What IS a strict claim
    here is the single-exponential locus -- parameter-free algebra, and the
    reason the statistic discriminates at all.
                                                  ratio   own null verdict
  THIS MODEL                                     0.7182     0.0833 inside
  Joos et al. 2013 Table 5                       0.7866     0.1676 -- the benchmark
  Spencer 2023 (2.05 %/yr over 295 ppm)          0.0166     0.0166 ON its own null, by construction
  Dengler & Reid 2023 (42-yr half-life)          0.0369     0.0369 ON its own null, by construction

  band [0.5930, 0.9788] -- CONSTRUCTED: Joos publishes no 5-95% range at
  TH 300, so Table 4's TH-100 relative width is borrowed. That is an
  assumption and it is stated, not silently adopted. The DISCRIMINATION does
  not rest on it: the one-box models sit 36x and 16x below even the
  loosest end, and every single exponential lies ON the null by construction.

  MUTATION TEST of this gate, because passing is not the same as working:
    a single exponential tuned to THIS MODEL's own IRF(100) = 0.2886
    would score 0.0833 and the gate must REJECT it: REJECTED. OK

  and the ASYMPTOTE, which is what the ratio is really testing:
    fraction still airborne at 300 yr: model 0.207 vs Joos T5 0.322
    Joos T5's t -> infinity limit is a0 = 0.2173; a single exponential's is 0.

